======================================================================
🚀 DAY 4 NOTES: INHERITANCE, POLYMORPHISM, ABCs, & COMPOSITION
======================================================================

1. INHERITANCE (THE "IS-A" RELATIONSHIP)

---

- Definition: A child class inherits all attributes and methods from a
  parent class. This prevents code repetition.
- The 'super()' Keyword: Used to call and run the parent class's
  constructor ('**init**') from inside the child class.
- AI Use-Case: You almost never write an AI model from scratch. You
  inherit from a base framework model (like PyTorch's 'nn.Module')
  and build your custom layers on top of it.

2. POLYMORPHISM (MANY FORMS)

---

- Definition: The ability for different classes to have methods with the
  exact same name but entirely different internal logic.
- Purpose: Allows you to write code that interacts with multiple types
  of objects without needing to know their specific class.
- AI Use-Case: You have a TextModel and an ImageModel. Both have a
  '.predict()' method. Your application can loop through a list of
  mixed models and call '.predict()' on all of them seamlessly.

3. ABSTRACT BASE CLASSES / ABC (THE ARCHITECTURAL CONTRACT)

---

- Definition: A strict master blueprint that cannot be instantiated
  directly. It forces all child classes to implement specific methods.
- Syntax: Uses the 'abc' module, inheriting from 'ABC', and tagging
  enforced methods with '@abstractmethod'.
- Purpose: Safety and standardization. It guarantees that any new model
  added to your pipeline by other team members won't break the app.

4. COMPOSITION (THE "HAS-A" RELATIONSHIP)

---

- Definition: Building a complex class by putting smaller, independent
  classes inside it as components, instead of relying on deep inheritance.
- Rule of Thumb: Prefer composition over inheritance when classes share
  components rather than a strict genetic identity.
- AI Use-Case: An AI training 'Pipeline' class isn't "born" from a
  DataLoader or a Model. Instead, it _has a_ DataLoader, _has a_ Model,
  and _has a_ Logger inside it to get the job done.

======================================================================
📌 KEY SHORTCUT SUMMARY FOR GIT OR NOTES:

- Inheritance: Child inherits parent code ("Is-A" model).
- Polymorphism: Same method name, different internal logic.
- ABC: Strict interface contract enforcing custom implementation.
- # Composition: Combining small objects into a larger machine ("Has-A").
